# Google Workspace Gmail

## When to use

User asked to search mail, read a message/thread, draft/reply/send, manage
labels, or manage filters. Prefer a connected Google Workspace MCP.

## MCP tool map

Pass `user_google_email` on every call as the connected MCP documents
(example pattern: `admin@nodadyoushutup.com`). Never invent message or
thread ids — resolve via search/get.

| Job | Tools |
| --- | --- |
| Search inbox | `search_gmail_messages` (`query`, optional `page_size`,
  `page_token`) — Gmail search syntax (`from:`, `subject:`, `newer_than:`,
  `label:`, `is:unread`, …) |
| Read one message | `get_gmail_message_content` (`message_id`, optional
  `body_format`) |
| Read many messages | `get_gmail_messages_content_batch` (`message_ids`) |
| Read one thread | `get_gmail_thread_content` (`thread_id`, optional
  `include_analysis`) |
| Read many threads | `get_gmail_threads_content_batch` (`thread_ids`) |
| Attachment bytes / URL | `get_gmail_attachment_content` (`message_id`,
  `attachment_id`) — do not paste large binaries into chat |
| List labels | `list_gmail_labels` |
| Create / update / delete label | `manage_gmail_label`
  (`action=create\|update\|delete`) |
| Label a message | `modify_gmail_message_labels` (`message_id`,
  `add_label_ids` / `remove_label_ids`) |
| Label many messages | `batch_modify_gmail_message_labels` (`message_ids`,
  add/remove label ids) |
| List filters | `list_gmail_filters` |
| Create / delete filter | `manage_gmail_filter` (`action=create\|delete`) |
| Draft (default outbound) | `draft_gmail_message` (`subject`, `body`; optional
  `to`/`cc`/`bcc`, `thread_id`, `in_reply_to`, `references`, `attachments`,
  `quote_original`, `from_email` Send-As alias) |
| Send (explicit verb) | `send_gmail_message` (`to`, `subject`, `body`; same
  optional threading/attachment fields) |

Outbound / label / filter mutates require an explicit verb — see
`google-workspace-safety`.

## Procedure

1. **Search first** — `search_gmail_messages` with a tight query before claiming
   empty results. Prefer ids from search hits over user-pasted guesses.
   **Done when** candidate message/thread ids are listed from MCP, or none
   match.
2. **Read lean** — use `get_gmail_message_content` / `get_gmail_thread_content`
   (or batch variants) for the ids you need. Summarize; redact secrets.
   **Done when** you have enough body/headers to answer or draft.
3. **Draft before send** — for new outbound or careful replies, call
   `draft_gmail_message` unless the user explicitly said send. Keep replies on
   the same `thread_id` when known; set `in_reply_to` / `references` when
   threading.
   **Done when** a draft id exists, or send was authorized and completed.
4. **Labels / filters** — resolve label ids via `list_gmail_labels` before
   modify; resolve filter ids via `list_gmail_filters` before delete. Create
   only when asked.
   **Done when** MCP confirms the change, or you refused for lack of verb.
5. **Evidence** — return message/thread ids, subject, and what changed (draft
   vs sent). **Done when** the reply cites MCP evidence and no unauthorized
   `send_gmail_message` ran.

## Defaults

1. Never invent message, thread, label, or filter ids.
2. Draft is the default for new outbound; send needs an explicit verb.
3. Do not auto-forward or bulk-send without an explicit ask naming recipients.
4. Prefer batch read tools when fetching several messages/threads.
5. Redact tokens, passwords, and full mailbox dumps from chat.
6. Attachments: prefer MCP attachment URLs / Drive download URLs over embedding
   raw base64 in chat.
7. Neighbor non-Workspace mail systems are out of scope for this plugin.

## Refuse

- Do not send, bulk-label, delete filters/labels, or invent recipients without
  an explicit ask this turn (`google-workspace-safety`).
- Do not claim mail was sent without a successful `send_gmail_message` result.
